       "The North-South corridor links Srinagar to Kanyakumari (4,076 km) and the East-West corridor links Silchar to Porbandar (3,640 km).",
       "These highway projects are implemented by the National Highways Authority of India (NHAI).",
       "State Highways, district roads and rural roads are built and maintained by states and local bodies.",
       "The Border Roads Organisation (BRO) was set up in 1960 — it builds roads in border areas.",
       "Indian Railways is Asia's largest and the world's fourth-largest rail network — route length was 67,956 km in 2019-20.",
       "On 16 April 1853 the first passenger train ran from Bori Bunder (Bombay) to Thane — 34 km covered by three engines (Sahib, Sindh, Sultan).",
