        "Compare the 1986 and 2019 consumer laws.",
        "The 1986 COPRA — three-tier — District (up to Rs 20 lakh), State (Rs 20 lakh–1 crore), National (above Rs 1 crore). The 2019 Act (from 20 July 2020) — District (up to Rs 1 crore), State (Rs 1–10 crore), National (above Rs 10 crore) — jurisdiction raised. New systems — CCPA (action against misleading ads), e-commerce coverage, product liability (manufacturer responsible), mediation cells (quick disposal). Similarity — the six rights in both. Conclusion — the 2019 law is the digital age's law — the answer to online market challenges.",
