       "The poet says society sleeps even while witnessing injustice — this sleep must break.",
       "The poem calls for awakening, awareness and resistance.",
       "It expresses sensitivity to the common person's suffering.",
       "The tone of satire and indignation is strong.",
       "The language is simple, colloquial and forceful.",
       "An example of contemporary poetry's pro-people style.",
       "The imagery is realistic.",
       "Exam fact: Dangwal's poetry is tied to the common man's concerns.",
       "Message: do not stay indifferent to injustice; wake up and raise your voice.",
       "Viren Dangwal was born just ten days before independence — on 5 August 1947.",
       "He received the Sahitya Akademi Award for 'Dushchakra mein Srashta'.",
       "His first poetry collection 'Isi Duniya Mein' (1991) won the Raghuvir Sahay Smriti Award.",
       "From 1971 he taught at Bareilly College.",
